      "title": "Eligibility and special enrollment",
      "narration": "HIPAA forbids a group health plan from basing eligibility or premium contributions on health status, medical history, genetic information, disability or claims experience. Everyone in the eligible class gets in on the same terms. HIPAA also created special enrollment periods: an employee who declined coverage may enroll midyear within 30 days after losing other coverage, or after marriage, birth, adoption or placement for adoption. Later law added 60 days for gaining or losing Medicaid or Children’s Health Insurance Program eligibility. Priya’s employee who waived coverage because of a spouse’s plan may join within 30 days if the spouse loses that plan.",
