      "title": "Guaranteed issue",
      "narration": "HIPAA required insurers in the small group market, then defined as 2 to 50 employees, to accept every small employer that applied and every eligible employee of that employer, regardless of health. It also defined eligible individuals, people leaving group coverage after at least 18 months with no gap of 63 days or more who had exhausted any COBRA, and required that they be able to obtain individual coverage; Maryland met that duty through a state high-risk pool before 2014. The Affordable Care Act extended guaranteed issue to all comprehensive individual and small group coverage, so today no one is denied for health reasons.",
