      "title": "Guaranteed renewability",
      "narration": "HIPAA requires insurers to renew group and individual coverage at the policyholder’s option. Nonrenewal is allowed only for nonpayment of premium, fraud or intentional misrepresentation, failure to meet participation or contribution rules in a group plan, movement outside the service area, or the insurer’s withdrawal from the entire market with 180 days’ notice. An insurer may not drop Priya’s group because claims ran high. Premiums may still change at renewal within the rating rules. This is the guaranteed renewable clause from Lesson 17 written into federal law for medical coverage.",
