      "title": "The privacy and security rules",
      "text": "HIPAA’s administrative simplification provisions require covered entities, including health plans and producers acting for them, to protect individually identifiable health information, use it only for treatment, payment and operations without authorization, and give individuals access to their records. Producers who handle applications and claims are bound by these rules through their agreements with carriers.",
